1. **A dual-pinion electric power steering system comprising:**

a rack bar having rack teeth and configured to transmit a steering force to steerable vehicle wheels;

a first pinion meshing with the rack teeth and operatively connectable to a steering input member;

a second pinion spaced from the first pinion along the rack bar and meshing with the rack teeth;

an electric motor operatively coupled to the second pinion to apply steering-assist torque to the rack bar through the second pinion;

a first pressing member arranged to press the rack bar toward the first pinion; and

a second pressing member arranged to press the rack bar toward the second pinion,

wherein the first pressing member has a lower rigidity than the second pressing member in respective directions in which the first and second pressing members press the rack bar.
